# WordPress SDLC and CI/CD

## Environments

| Env        | Where                                            | Purpose                              |
| ---------- | ------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------ |
| local      | `wp-env` (Docker), `npm run env:start`, :8888    | All development and visual QA        |
| production | Hostinger `~/domains/egi-optics.com/public_html` | Live site; changed only by deploy job or reviewed WP-CLI scripts |

There is no staging yet: production deploys are therefore **backup-first** and every change must be
verified locally (screenshots desktop + mobile) before the PR is opened.

## Development loop

1. `composer install && npm install`, then `npm run env:start` (theme + plugin are bind-mounted).
2. Work only inside `wp-content/themes/egi-optics`, `wp-content/plugins/egi-optics-core`, `scripts/`.
3. Before pushing: `npm run lint` (css, js, php) and `npm run validate` (theme.json / block.json).
4. Never edit files on the server by hand or via wp-admin theme/plugin editors (`DISALLOW_FILE_EDIT` is on).

## CI (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`) - required to merge

PHP syntax (parallel-lint) -> PHPCS WordPress-Extra + Docs + PHPCompatibilityWP 8.2 -> stylelint -> eslint -> JSON validation.
A failing check blocks the merge; do not disable rules to get green, fix the code or add a justified `// phpcs:ignore <sniff> -- reason`.

## CD (`.github/workflows/deploy.yml`) - on push to `main`

1. `scripts/server/backup.sh` over SSH: `mysqldump | gzip` + tar of the current theme/plugin into `~/backups/egi-optics/<timestamp>/` (keeps last 10).
2. `rsync -az --delete` **only** `wp-content/themes/egi-optics/` and `wp-content/plugins/egi-optics-core/` (dev files excluded via `.rsync-exclude`).
3. `scripts/server/post-deploy.sh`: activate theme/plugin idempotently, `wp rewrite flush`, `wp cache flush`, `wp litespeed-purge all`.
4. Health check: HTTP 200 on `/`, `/products/`, `/news/`; the job fails loudly otherwise.

Secrets (`HOSTINGER_SSH_KEY`, `HOSTINGER_HOST`, `HOSTINGER_PORT`, `HOSTINGER_USER`, `HOSTINGER_PATH`) live only in GitHub Actions secrets.

## Updates and maintenance

- WordPress core, third-party plugins: test the update locally in `wp-env` first, then apply on the server with WP-CLI (`wp plugin update <slug>`) after a backup. Never patch vendor code; wrap behaviour with hooks in `egi-optics-core`.
- Keep the plugin count minimal; every new plugin needs a justification in the PR and must be free/GPL and actively maintained.
- Security baseline: HTTPS-only URLs, `DISALLOW_FILE_EDIT`, XML-RPC disabled, no file editing in wp-admin, least-privilege users, Solid Security kept active.

## Rollback

Re-run the deploy workflow from the previous tag (`workflow_dispatch` with `ref`), or restore the
matching backup with the commands in `docs/DEPLOYMENT_RUNBOOK.md`. Database restores are a last
resort and must be announced first.
